  Prefab: {fileID: 1564578960232786664, guid: fb939d6c10b2b254da62164302f28f6e, type: 3}
  TitleText: Document
  BodyText: "A\u2014\r\nYou won\u2019t believe this, but I\u2019m at your aunt\u2019s
    house! I wanted to surprise you\u2014guess you had the same idea. What\u2019s
    that quote? \u201CIf then true lovers have been ever crossed . . . \u201D  Can\u2019t
    remember the rest. Maybe it\u2019ll come to me.   \r\n \r\nI heard you solved
    the first puzzle! You\u2019re incredible, Astrid. (And just like Perseus . .
    . smart, brave. Is it too soon to say I told you so?) The next puzzle is Hercules.
    You probably already know the story: Hercules, the half-god son of Zeus, went
    crazy and wreaked a bunch of havoc. As punishment, the Oracle sent him out on
    ten labors. That\u2019s where we get the phrase \u201Ca Herculean task.\u201D
    It means something hard. Something that seems impossible.\r\n \r\nLately I feel
    sort of like Hercules. I need to travel to all the STAR stations in the Midwest
    and update their tech. Not sure how long it\u2019ll take. I don\u2019t want to
    freak you out, but this is big. If it works, it\u2019ll change everything. I
    just hope we\u2019re not too late.\r\n \r\nWill explain more later. Running out
    of light and ink. When my journey is done, I\u2019ll meet you at World\u2019s
    End.\r\n-E\r\n \r\nP.S. Remembered it! \u201CIf then true lovers ever have been
    crossed, it stands as an edict in destiny . . .  as due to love as thoughts and
    dreams and sighs.\u201D\r\n"
